# Controls what `gcloud run deploy --source` uploads to Cloud Build.
#
# This is a separate mechanism from .dockerignore: gcloud decides what leaves this machine,
# .dockerignore decides what enters an image layer. Both must exclude .secrets/ — relying on
# gcloud's implicit fallback to .gitignore would be an accident waiting to happen.
#
# Note the Dockerfile itself must NOT be excluded here: Cloud Build needs it.

# === Secrets — must never leave the machine ===
.secrets/
.env
*.env
appsettings.*.local.json

# === Version control ===
.git/
.gitignore
.github/

# === Build output ===
**/bin/
**/obj/
artifacts/
*.user
.vs/
*.trx
coverage.cobertura.xml

# === Internal development ecosystem — not part of the product (ADR-007) ===
_hilo/
_patron/
Documentos_Base/
ecosystem.config.json
AGENTS.md
GEMINI.md
.agents/
.gemini/
BRIEF_STRIPBOARD.md
RUNBOOK.md
EVOLUTIVOS.md

# === Python agent layer — not part of the web image ===
agents/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# === Not needed to build the web app ===
tests/
